  "thesis": "The latest lagged Cboe SKEW close identifies unusually expensive perceived equity left-tail risk that is complementary to the VIX variance level. Holding BTC only when SKEW is at or below its prior-252-business-day percentile threshold may avoid cross-market tail-risk transmission and improve Calmar and drawdown while preserving enough BTC upside after fees and adverse slippage.",
  "economic_rationale": "The policy is valuable only if avoiding the highest option-implied left-tail states reduces BTC drawdown and underwater risk enough to offset missed rallies and round-trip costs. Positive return alone is insufficient: Design, Validation, annual breadth, Calmar, upside capture, terminal inventory and both neighboring percentiles must support the same mechanism.",
